#: views/help.html.php:2
msgid "Hostel PRO for WordPress"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:4
msgid ""
"This is a Premium plugin for managing hostels, BNB sites, and small hotel "
"sites. You get an area where to manage your available rooms and prices, and "
"the bookings made by visitors. Start with the main settings page to set up "
"your booking mode, currency etc."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:6
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:9
msgid ""
"Visit the <a href=\"%s\">settings page</a> to set up booking methods, "
"booking form URL etc."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:10
msgid "Create your rooms."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:11
msgid ""
"If there are dates when your hostel does not work add them in the "
"\"Unavailable dates\" page."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:12
msgid ""
"Publish some of the shortcodes below, or the room calendar shortcodes from "
"the \"Manage Rooms\" page so your guests can see your room availability."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:13
msgid "You are ready to get accept guests!"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:16
msgid "Shortcodes"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:19
msgid ""
"will display a table with your available rooms. A date selector on the top "
"lets the user choose dates of their visit and then the rooms list is "
"updated. If you have enabled booking in your Hostel settings page, the table "
"will also show \"Book\" button when appropriate. The button will "
"automaically load the booking form."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:20
msgid ""
"This shorcode accepts arguments which allow you to specify whether room "
"title, description, type or bathroom information should be shown in the "
"table. Each argument can be set to 0 (means \"do not show\") and 1 (means "
"\"show\"):"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:22
msgid ""
"Show / hide the table initially when loading the page (it will always be "
"shown after clicking the availability button). Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:23
msgid ""
"Set to 1 if you want the availability checking form to be displayed "
"horizontally. Defaults to 0 (vertical form)."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:24
msgid "Show / hide room titles. Defaults to 0."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:25
msgid "Show / hide room descriptions. Defaults to 0."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:26
msgid "Show / hide room types. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:27
msgid "Show / hide bahtroom information. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:28
msgid ""
"This will automatically group rooms of same type / gender / number of beds / "
"price. For example if you have 3 mixed dorm rooms with 8 beds and same "
"price, only one will be shown. In cases when there is different number of "
"available rooms, our smart logic engine will choose the one with the best "
"availability. Learn more below. This parameter defaults to 0."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:29
msgid "The maximum number of days that can be selected. Defaults to 5."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:30
msgid ""
"Whether to switch the \"availability\" table cells to vertical display to "
"avoid making the table too wide. By default this setting is off. Pass number "
"of days after which the cells should turn vertical."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:31
msgid ""
"By default this shortcode shows each of the selected dates along with the "
"availability for it. You can hide this by passing \"hide_dates=1\"."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:32
msgid ""
"Defines how rooms are sorted. Possible values: title or price. Defaults to "
"\"price\"."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:33
msgid ""
"Defines the direction of sorting - asceding or descending. Possible values: "
"asc or desc. Defaults to \"asc\"."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:35
msgid ""
"For example using the shortcode like this: <b>%s</b> will generate a table "
"that shows room titles and descriptions withouth \"type\" information."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:37
msgid ""
"displays a generic booking form with a drop-down selector for choosing room, "
"and a date selector. If you use the [hostelpro-list] shortcode you most "
"probably do not need this one because the booking form is automatically "
"generated."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:40
msgid "How the smart logic chooses which room to show when rooms are grouped?"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:42
msgid ""
"When you use the [hostelpro-list] code with group_rooms=1 (like this: "
"[hostelpro_list group_rooms=1]), the following logic will be used:"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:44
msgid ""
"The room that has available beds for more of the user-selected days will be "
"preferred."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:45
msgid ""
"In case of a tie the room that has more available beds in the least "
"available day will be preferred."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:46
msgid ""
"In case of a tie the room with the highest sum of available beds in the user-"
"selected days will be preferred."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:49
msgid ""
"This algo is used by the most popular hostel listing sites so we decided to "
"follow it."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:51
msgid "Translating"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:53
msgid ""
"If you want to translate this plugin check out <a href=\"%s\" target=\"_blank"
"\">this guide</a>. The language template file is available in the plugin "
"folder and called hostelpro.pot. Our plugin textdomain is \"hostelpro\" and "
"you have to place your .po and .mo files in folder languages/"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:55
msgid "Modifying the views/templates"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:57
msgid "Only for advanced users!"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:59
msgid ""
"You can safely customize all files from the \"views\" folders by placing "
"their copies in your theme folder. Simply create folder \"hostelpro\" <b>in "
"your theme root folder</b> and copy the files you want to custom from \"views"
"\" folder directly there."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:61
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:64
msgid ""
"If you are using the Twenty Fourteen theme, you should create folder "
"\"hostelpro\" under it so the structure will now be something like <b>wp-"
"content/themes/twentyfourteen/hostelpro</b>. (The files that are above the "
"new \"hostelpro\" folder should remain where they are)."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:65
msgid ""
"Then if you want to modify the \"Manage Rooms\" page copy the file rooms.php "
"from the plugin \"views\" folder and place it in the new \"hostelpro\" "
"folder so you will have  <b>wp-content/themes/twentyfourteen/hostelpro/rooms."
"php</b>"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:68
msgid ""
"Don't worry if you use modified WordPress directory structure and don't have "
"'wp-content' folder. The trick will work with any structure as long as you "
"follow the same logic."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:70
msgid ""
"Then feel free to modify the code, but of course be careful not to mess with "
"the PHP or Javascript inside. This will let you change the design and even "
"part of the functionality and not lose these changes when the plugin is "
"upgraded. Be careful: we can not provide support for your custom versions of "
"our views."
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:72
msgid "Extending"
msgstr ""

#: views/help.html.php:74
msgid ""
"If you want to extend the plugin with custom functions our <a href=\"%s\" "
"target=\"_blank\">Developers API</a> may come handy. Please let us know if "
"you need a hook or filter to be added."
msgstr ""

